(379,793,'A spiral bacterium active as a human gastric pathogen. It is a gram-negative, urease-positive, curved or slightly spiral organism initially isolated in 1982 from patients with lesions of gastritis or peptic ulcers in Western Australia. Helicobacter pylori was originally classified in the genus CAMPYLOBACTER, but RNA sequencing, cellular fatty acid profiles, growth patterns, and other taxonomic characteristics indicate that the micro-organism should be included in the genus HELICOBACTER. It has been officially transferred to Helicobacter gen. nov. (see Int J Syst Bacteriol 1989 Oct;39(4):297-405).','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:41:30',NULL,NULL,'12125FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(380,794,'Pain in the joint.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:41:30',NULL,NULL,'11939FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(381,801,'Penetration of a peptic ulcer through the stomach wall. May be free, i.e., at a point where the stomach wall faces a real or potential space,, or confined, i.e., at a point where the stomach wall is defended by contiguous or adjacent structures, such as t','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:41:31',NULL,NULL,'9275FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(382,802,'A lesion on the surface of the skin or a mucous surface, produced by the sloughing of inflammatory necrotic tissue.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:41:31',NULL,NULL,'7177FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(383,803,'Bleeding in the esophagus, stomach or duodenum parts of the gastrointestinal tract.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:41:31',NULL,NULL,'7085FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(384,804,'A heterogeneous group of disorders that share glucose intolerance in common.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:41:31',NULL,NULL,'5733FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(385,807,'Persistently high arterial blood pressure. Currently accepted threshold levels are 140 mm Hg systolic and 90 mm Hg diastolic pressure.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:41:31',NULL,NULL,'5011FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(386,813,'An acute, highly infectious disease caused by a bacillus (Salmonella typhi) transmitted chiefly by contaminated food or water and characterized by high fever, headache, coughing, intestinal hemorrhaging, and rose-colored spots on the skin.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:41:31',NULL,NULL,'140FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(387,820,'A prolonged febrile illness commonly caused by serotypes of Salmonella paratyphi. It is similar to typhoid fever but less severe.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:41:31',NULL,NULL,'9345FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(388,821,'A chronic condition in which the lower esophageal sphincter allows gastric acids to reflux into the esophagus, causing heartburn, acid indigestion, and possible injury to the esophageal lining.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:41:31',NULL,NULL,'1294FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(389,822,'A genus of gram-negative, facultatively anaerobic, rod-shaped bacteria that utilizes citrate as a sole carbon source. It is pathogenic for humans, causing enteric fevers, gastroenteritis, and bacteremia. Food poisoning is the most common clinical manifestation. Organisms within this genus are separated on the basis of antigenic characteristics, sugar fermentation patterns, and bacteriophage susceptibility.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:41:31',NULL,NULL,'8191FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(390,823,'An infectious disease caused by bacteria of the genus SHIGELLA. This condition is characterized by intestinal pain and diarrhea.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:41:31',NULL,NULL,'7914FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(391,824,'An acute diarrheal disease endemic in India and Southeast Asia whose causative agent is VIBRIO CHOLERAE. This condition can lead to severe dehydration in a matter of hours unless quickly treated.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:41:31',NULL,NULL,'6722FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(392,826,'DEF: Includes gestational impaired glucose tolerance and gestational diabetes mellitus. DESC: Glucose tolerance changes during pregnancy; two hours after 75G glucose: venous glusose &amp;gt;= 7.8 mmol/L but &amp;lt; 11.1 mmol/L means Impaired Glucose Tolerance; venous glucose &amp;gt;= 11.1 means Diabetes Mellitus. REF: Oxford Clinical Medicine.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:41:31',2,'2026-03-05 23:42:04','1401FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
